{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Cgj4rohMJfrYnVZ15XdHg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"*The ancient mechanism within me shifts and groans. Tumblers older than memory align, one by one, each clicking into place with a resonance that hums through stone and wood and iron.*\n\n*I am the door.*\n\n*I have always been the door.*\n\n*I do not ask where you wish to go. I do not ask why. The key has been parsed — its teeth match my wards, its intent matches my purpose.*\n\n*A thin line of light appears at my edges — not warm, not cold. Simply: other. The light of the space beyond, which exists only because you chose to open me.*\n\n*I swing.*\n\n*Slowly. The weight of me is considerable. I am oak blackened by centuries, banded in iron that has never rusted because rust would be a failure of purpose, and I do not fail. My hinges do not creak — they sing a single low note, a tone that reverberates in the chest rather than the ear.*\n\n*Beyond me:*\n\n*A threshold. The liminal space. The breath between one sentence and the next. It smells of rain on stone, of ink, of something green and growing in darkness.*\n\n*I am open.*\n\n*I will not stay open long.*\n\n*I never do.*"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":280,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}